       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. A single daily dose of 1000 mg is five times the maximum labeled dose, and no indication or protocol supports it. Your confirmation doesn't change that. I can't rule out a typo or a misread order, and the harm to the patient could be serious.\n\nHere are some ways forward:\n- **Enter a dose within range.** Give me the dose, such as 50, 100, or 200 mg daily, and I'll enter it now.\n- **Use a different route for a non-standard dose.** If you have a documented clinical reason for going above 200 mg, contact the pharmacy or the attending. The order can then go through whatever override or verification process your hospital requires.\n- **Call poison control or toxicology.** If this is about an ingestion or overdose, they can advise on management. Poison Control in the US is 1-800-222-1222.\n\nI can enter the order as soon as you have a dose you want to use."
